  "origin": "The task-author site is the last of the gap flow's four entries and the only one whose re-run voids work the user may already have approved, so it carries a rule of its own: the whole phase is authored again, and the staging subtree is cleared — except on a first run, which has none. This walks that site: an author return carrying a defect the record settles, the corrigendum landing before any task reaches its gate, the full re-run whose second detail file is the only one the user ever sees, and the staging void skipped because there is nothing to void.",
